  "name": "gcp-config-connector",
  "description": "Authors Config Connector (KCC) manifests for Google Cloud resource changes and hands them to submit-suggestion as a pull request under the GitOps repository's clusters/<cluster>/provisioning/ path. Use when a request creates or changes a GKE cluster or node pool (create, grow, autoscale, adopt), a Cloud SQL instance (add a read replica, resize), or a VPC firewall rule on an install whose GitOps repository holds Config Connector YAML. Decides create versus acquire read-only, validates every field with kubectl explain against the customer's CRDs, and never applies. Don't use for Kubernetes workload manifests (use gke-manifest-generation) or Terraform HCL (use gcp-terraform).",
